<section class="section"><div class="container article-layout">
  <article class="prose article" data-article>
    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0,0,0,0.06); border: 1px solid var(--border); background: #0f172a;">
      <img src="{{ asset('assets/img/blogs/what-to-prepare-software-development.svg') }}" alt="What to prepare before contacting a software development company" style="width: 100%; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; display: block;">
    </div>
    <p>You do not need a polished specification to start a conversation. But a little preparation helps both sides. Here is what is most useful.</p>
<h2 id="a-short-description-of-the-business-and-the-problem">A short description of the business and the problem</h2>
<p>Who are your customers, and what is going wrong or missing today? Two paragraphs are plenty.</p>
<h2 id="who-will-use-the-software">Who will use the software</h2>
<p>List the types of users, such as customers, staff, managers or partners, and roughly how many of each.</p>
<h2 id="examples-you-like-and-dislike">Examples you like and dislike</h2>
<p>Links to websites or apps with features or styles you admire help communicate more than long explanations. Mention what you dislike too.</p>
<h2 id="existing-systems-and-data">Existing systems and data</h2>
<p>Note any current software, spreadsheets or websites involved, and whether data needs to be moved across.</p>
<h2 id="your-timeline-and-budget-range">Your timeline and budget range</h2>
<p>Even a rough range helps a partner suggest an approach that fits, such as phasing the work. Being open about budget usually leads to better advice, not higher quotes.</p>
<h2 id="decision-making-and-content">Decision-making and content</h2>
<p>Who approves designs and features? Who will supply text, images and data? Delays here are one of the most common causes of late projects.</p>
<h2 id="questions-to-ask-the-company">Questions to ask the company</h2>
<ul><li>Who will actually do the work, and who will be my contact?</li><li>How do you handle changes in scope?</li><li>What happens after launch: support, hosting and updates?</li><li>Who owns the code and the data?</li></ul>
<h2 id="ready-to-talk">Ready to talk?</h2>
<p>Our <a href="/start-a-project">project enquiry form</a> is designed around these points. Share what you can; we will ask about the rest.</p></article>
